    "case_id": "amb1-case02-nonprofit-scale",
    "focal_region": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne028\tI dislike the implication that volunteers have to prove their excitement before we take a risk.\ne029\tThey already give us evenings after work.\ne030\tOur lead has built this program with me, and she thinks I keep moving the standard whenever she brings an ambitious idea.\ne031\tLast year I said we needed participant demand; now Willow Hub brought demand and I am asking for staffing certainty.\ne032\tMaybe I am protecting myself from being responsible for a messy expansion.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne033\tYou may be cautious, but the standard has also changed because the proposal became more concrete.\ne034\tDemand answered one question and revealed others.\ne035\tStill, if your colleague experiences every new question as a veto, the process is damaging trust.\ne036\tIt may help to name what uncertainty you are willing to carry rather than asking for certainty.\ne037\tFor example, you might accept variable attendance and some volunteer gaps while refusing to launch without one accountable local coordinator.\ne038\tThat makes the threshold debatable instead of endlessly movable.\n[Turn 5 USER]\ne039\tThere is funding context too.\ne040\tA foundation officer told me informally that geographic reach would make our next application easier to explain.\ne041\tShe did not promise anything, and the current grant pays for curriculum improvement, not expansion.\ne042\tIf we delay, we can improve the drop-in materials and volunteer training.\ne043\tIf we expand, we have a stronger story but might be stretching restricted work into the background.\ne044\tI am embarrassed by how much the application narrative is affecting me.\n[Turn 5 ASSISTANT]\ne045\tIt is reasonable to care about future funding, but an easier story is not the same as a stronger program or a likely grant.\ne046\tTreat the foundation comment as one input, not financing.\ne047\tThe sharper conflict is that curriculum work may improve both sites later, while a second site may create evidence and relationships you cannot get from preparation alone.\ne048\tEither path can support the mission; the risk is pretending that one path offers both learning and stability without giving something up.",
